<Base title="About"><section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About ICONA</div><h1>Working together to understand ocean change.</h1><p>The International CO₂ Natural Analogues Network connects researchers and research sites around the world.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>Our purpose</h2><p class="lead">Natural laboratories provide opportunities to study marine organisms and ecosystems experiencing environmental conditions that can offer insight into future oceans.</p><p>ICONA aims to strengthen international cooperation, comparative research, coordinated methods and knowledge exchange across these research systems.</p></div><div class="feature"><div><span>◎</span><h3>Connect · Compare · Collaborate</h3></div></div></div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container text-width"><h2>Coordination & contact</h2><p>This section will include the network's official governance, contacts, and acknowledgements. Please verify the text with ICONA coordinators before public launch.</p><div class="notice">Contact email and funding acknowledgements intentionally left blank until confirmed.</div></div></section></Base>
